298
00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:22.720
Randy shared that there are two kinds of music rights.

299
00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:28.720
There are sync rights, which is where you're going to play a song by the original artist,

300
00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:29.800
and that's all.

301
00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:31.560
You're just going to hear their song.

302
00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:38.440
But then there are master rights, and that's what you need if a character is going to sing

303
00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:39.720
or hum a song.

304
00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:41.900
Sort of do their interpretation.

305
00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:42.560
Yes.

306
00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:43.180
Of the artiSt.

